* Noteworthy changes in Basalt Deep Learning 0.1 (2026-10-31)

** Initial release of Basalt Deep Learning (0.1.0), built upon the Bellows
   machine-learning engine.

** Core Tensor and Backend Engine:
   - N-dimensional strided `basalt::Tensor` with zero-copy slicing,
     transposition, permutation, reshaping, and multi-dimensional
     broadcasting across `f16`, `bf16`, `f32`, `f64`, `i32`, `i64`, `u8`,
     and `bool`.
   - Zero-allocation power-of-2 caching slab pools for both CPU (`aligned_alloc`
     via `hyper_math::slab_buffer`) and CUDA unified memory
     (`cuMemAllocManaged`).
   - CPU backend dispatching through Bellows / Hyper Math AVX2+FMA and OpenMP
     8-P-core parallel kernels, plus runtime-loaded CUDA driver (`libcuda.so`),
     cuBLAS (`libcublas.so`), and NVRTC JIT PTX kernels (`libnvrtc.so`).

** Dynamic Reverse-Mode Autograd:
   - Dynamic computational graph engine supporting higher-order derivatives
     (`create_graph = true`), `No_Grad_Guard`, `Enable_Grad_Guard`, and
     activation checkpointing.

** Neural Network Modules, Optimizers, and Schedulers:
   - Complete `basalt::nn` module library (`Linear`, `Conv1d`/`2d`/`3d` with
     `im2col` + GEMM forward and backward kernels, `Conv_Transpose2d`,
     pooling, `Batch_Norm`, fused single-pass `Layer_Norm` on CPU and CUDA,
     `Group_Norm`, `Instance_Norm1d`/`2d`/`3d`, `RMS_Norm`, fused `gelu` and
     `softmax` on CPU and CUDA, online-softmax FlashAttention
     `Multihead_Attention`, `Transformer_Encoder`, `Transformer_Decoder`,
     `RNN`, `LSTM`, `GRU`, `Rotary_Embedding` (`RoPE`), `KV_Cache`,
     `Embedding`, `Dropout`).
   - Optimizers (`SGD`, `Adam`, `AdamW`, `RMSprop`, `Adagrad`, `LAMB` with
     fused NVRTC GPU and vectorized CPU updates), losses (`MSE_Loss`,
     `L1_Loss`, `Smooth_L1_Loss`, `Huber_Loss`, `NLL_Loss`,
     `Cross_Entropy_Loss`, `BCE_With_Logits_Loss`, `KL_Div_Loss`,
     `Cosine_Embedding_Loss`), and schedulers (`Step_LR`, `Exponential_LR`,
     `Multi_Step_LR`, `Cosine_Annealing_LR`, `One_Cycle_LR`,
     `Linear_Warmup_LR`, `Reduce_LR_On_Plateau`).

** Data Pipeline, Serialization, Trainer, C ABI, CLI, and Python:
   - Deterministic, multi-threaded prefetching `Data_Loader` and POSIX
     memory-mapped datasets.
   - Versioned self-describing checkpoints, Safetensors import/export, and
     ONNX import/export.
   - Lightning-style `basalt::Trainer` with callbacks, early stopping,
     checkpoint resume, pluggable loggers, and data-parallel training.
   - Stable C ABI (`libbasalt-c`), CLI tools (`basalt-train`,
     `basalt-inspect`, `basalt-convert`), and optional Python bindings.

** Benchmark Results (`bench/bench_basalt` on Intel Core i7-12700K & RTX 3070):
   - `matmul` (256x256 fp32, CPU AVX2+FMA)        :  0.111 ms/iter (303.380 GFLOP/s)
   - `Conv2d` (4x8x16x16 -> 16, k=3, CPU)         :  0.088 ms/iter
   - `MLP` (32x64->128->32 fwd+bwd, CPU)          :  0.205 ms/iter
   - `Transformer_Encoder` (4x16x32, CPU)         :  0.341 ms/iter
   - `CUDA matmul` (1024x1024 fp32, RTX 3070)     :  0.209 ms/iter (10261.162 GFLOP/s)
   - `CUDA TensorCore` (2048x2048 fp16, RTX 3070) :  0.504 ms/iter (34109.968 GFLOP/s)

